Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2


&nbsp;
Morning All 
&nbsp;
I have slightly tweaked the letter as attached (amend for repetition and raise one comment). On Theo’s comments (focussing on those that require further thought and comment our side)
&nbsp;
I haven't been party to the detail of Gramercy's arrangements with PG save that I have seen what is in Alinia 1, so can't help on whether this detail is correct/comprehensive. What is important
 to say is that given the ATE shortfall there is a real risk that the funding agreements between PG and Gramercy will eventually be disclosed to the court. It is critical that this account presents a straightforward and accurate picture of Gramercy's funding.
We are checking internally to make sure that we are comfortable with the statement that “the September ($30m) Tranche can contractually be used only for the
 NOx Group Litigations.” I believe this is correct on the basis that the facility must be spent in line with the funder approved budget and that budget only provides for spend against the Nox litigation and proportionate share of firm operating costs, but I
 am not sure how clear this will be to demonstrate through the actual contracts.
&nbsp;
You need to be careful that this is absolutely aligned with what is said about the Gramercy additional funding in Alicia Alinia’s recent First Witness Statement. Particularly she says the 30m
 additional is reserved to only be spent on these proceedings while the 65m is also for wider overheads. We need to be consistent here.
@Neil
 Pigott ?
&nbsp;
Are there any other funders of the litigation, including historic, who might be said to contribute to the Claimant’s costs? I distantly recall I have seen mention of another funder - but is that
 historic?
We said the below in Tom’s March witness statement, this would have been in relation to NorthWall.

&nbsp;
The funds provided by Gramercy were used, in part, to repay previous debt finance provided to Pogust Goodhead, which has been superseded by the funding.
&nbsp;
We have not disclosed the $140m G2 facility which is exhausted and did not provide funding for the Nox litigation (save for overheads in the same way as G3)
&nbsp;
Other potentially relevant funders which we discussed yesterday include Locke, Fulcrum, DRS, and Pogust Goodhead LLC, who provided funding for Nox client aggregation
 costs (marketing) 
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Tom
&nbsp;
