Please find attached first draft of the breakdown. &nbsp;This is by no means the final product as we still need to undertake a few more tasks that are listed below.&nbsp; However, this should give you
 an indication of the amount that is to be claimed.&nbsp; There are a few things which your team/PG will need to consider and advise us on whether these needs amending in the breakdown.
&nbsp;

There are a number of foreign lawyers who are said to be Grade A/B fee earners and as such have claimed rates in line with those grades.&nbsp; However,
 the guidelines are clear in specifying that those who can claim a Grade A and B rates are
“Solicitors and legal executives with over 8(or 4 for Grade B) years’ experience”.&nbsp; Therefore, in these circumstances we usually state that the fee earners are a Grade C but claim the Grade A rate.&nbsp; However, in this case, we do not believe that this
 is possible as assume the retainer would specify the Grade and the rate to be charged rather than specific fee earners.&nbsp; As a result, if we are to keep them claimed at a Grade A rate, it is likely that this will be criticised by the other side.&nbsp; However, if
 we claim them at the Grade C rate, this will reduce the costs claim.&nbsp; Please can you advise on how you wish to proceed.
[I am bit puzzled by this comment, because it implies that we may be claiming a hypothetical rather than an actual rate in respect of foreign lawyers. Should we not just be claiming the actual rates charged by the foreign lawyers? The
 question whether that was a reasonable rate and in line with guideline rates is a matter for assessment, but I don’t think that we need to second guess this at this stage. Likewise, I assume that for English solicitors, we are claiming by reference to the
 actual rates at which they were charged, not hypothetical rates, right?]Can you please advise on whether there are any other Claim Numbers on this matter which need to be included on the front pageCounsel and disbursements have been included as per PG’s analysis of the same, however, we do query why there was a disbursement payment to
 slaughter and may (see row 48 of tab “disbs”) – if this is a share in a particular disbursement, we will need to know what this was.&nbsp; Please can PG clarify as to what date counsel and disbursements fees have been included up to.&nbsp; Counsel’s fees in particular
 to appear low in comparison to the profit costs, therefore, we request that this is checked.On the fee earner list provided by PG, there were some individuals who were not on the list, therefore, we have taken their rates from the
 ledgers.&nbsp; Where these fee earners were stated to be Grade A, we have assumed that they were to be claiming Grade A3 rate.&nbsp; As such, we recommend that PG review the fee earner tab (“FE”) and confirm that the grades claimed are accurate.
&nbsp;
