00. A list of partners is available on our website. For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Tuesday, September 30, 2025 17:11To:&nbsp;Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jamie Macfarlane &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Many thanks for your email Sarah. We will approach insurers in relation to the below.&nbsp;Is there a deadline by which the insurance would need to be secured by?&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Litigation Risk, Cyber, Directors &amp; Officers, Financial Institutions, Mergers &amp; Acquisitions, Professional Indemnity, and Operational Risks within WTW.Part of our wider risk solutions capabilities at WTW&nbsp;At WTW we work flexibly - whilst you may receive emails from me out of working hours, I do not expect a response or action outside your own working hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;30 September 2025 10:25To:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;jonathan.simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jamie Macfarlane &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;Dear James and Jonathan,I hope you're well.I am writing regarding the Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation, specifically regarding the viability of securing additional LOI coverage through further excess layer insurance policies.Following the handing down of the judgment (10th September 2025) after the Second Costs Management Hearing (15-16 July 2025), the Defendants have revisited their position on applications for security for costs. We have therefore undertaken a further review of the potential adverse costs resulting from the Tranche 3 Quantum Trial and the Second General Budget.&nbsp;Previously, our assessment of ATE sufficiency was calculated on the following basis:60% of the Defendants’ claimed incurred costs;60% of the Defendants’ claimed budgeted costs; and100% of approved future costs to Spring 2026.Given the level of incurred costs&nbsp;and the criticisms between Defendants regarding their figures, we consider that the sufficiency calculation can be revised downwards without materially affecting the adequacy of coverage. We propose the following revised basis:50% of the Defendants’ claimed incurred costs;50% of the Defendants’ claimed budgeted costs; and100% of approved future costs to 31 July 2026.On this revised basis, the following GLOs fall below the proposed coverage threshold:&nbsp;Mercedes&nbsp;-£953,580.35Ford-£838,961.27Renault-Nissan-£2,535,219.93PCD-£149,635.79Toyota-£136,927.40&nbsp;We would be grateful for your confirmation on whether additional excess layer coverage can be secured for these cases, specifically for&nbsp;Mercedes, Ford, and Renault-Nissan.We look forward to hearing from you as soon as possible.Kind regards,&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Sarah&nbsp;BinghamLegal&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7484&nbsp;085&nbsp;187This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our website. For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.&nbsp;______________________________________________________________________For information pertaining to WTW's email confidentiality and monitoring policy, usage restrictions, or for specific company registration and regulatory status information, please visit https://www.wtwco.com/en-gb/notices/legal-disclaimersIf the Client provides WTW with, or makes available to WTW, any information which constitutes ‘personal data’ (including any ‘sensitive personal data’ or ‘Special Category’ data), as defined in the General Data Protection Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2016/679) as amended and incorporated into UK law under the UK European Union (Withdrawal) Act 2018 (&quot;Regulation&quot;), WTW will treat such information at all times in accordance with the Regulation in the manner described within WTW’s Privacy Notice, which can be found online at https://www.wtwco.com/en-gb/notices/transactional-advisory-services-privacy-notice.At WTW, we provide data-driven, insight-led solutions in the areas of people, risk and capital that make your organization more resilient, motivate your workforce, and maximize performance. WTW has offices in 140 countries and markets. For a complete list of office locations, please click hereYou may receive direct marketing communications from WTW. If so, you have the right to opt out of these communications. You can opt out of these communications by emailing unsubscribe@wtwco.com&nbsp;[ELD-DEF].You may access a copy of WTW's privacy notice by clicking here. ______________________________________________________________________"}

