Thanks @Riceman, Sarah @Urquhart, Charles for your feedback below. &nbsp;Unless there are any objections, I will hit send at 3pm.&nbsp;Thank youR&nbsp;​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From: James Newton &lt;James.Newton@pallasllp.com&gt;Date: Friday, 17 October 2025 at 13:58To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;, Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;, Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Urquhart, Charles &lt;charles.urquhart@clydeco.com&gt;Subject: RE: ReportCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;All,&nbsp;Further to Matt’s email below, please see attached a revised draft from Raminder.&nbsp;Charlie – there are two items that we have highlighted in yellow for your additional input.&nbsp;Kind regards,James&nbsp;--- FROM RAMINDER ---&nbsp;Hi Mike,Thank you for your email.&nbsp; I have also been provided with your emails to Alicia from today regarding a potential article in The Times, suggestions of criminal conduct and concerns over Gramercy.&nbsp; This email responds to them together.As previously communicated to you, we will not be releasing you from your notice period.&nbsp; Your continued attempts to leave earlier than your contract allows are proving disruptive to our efforts to safeguard good governance within the firm.&nbsp; In addition, your conduct threatens to seriously damage morale and be more disruptive than helpful, taking account of the best interests of our clients.We are, therefore, minded to put you give you the option of being placed on paid leave for the remainder of your notice period.&nbsp; We would view that as regrettable since we are in the midst of the PDD Trial and would much prefer to have you remain working on the team.&nbsp; However, your continued conduct threatens to seriously damage morale and be more disruptive than helpful, taking account of the best interests of our clients.We therefore give you the choice of either to (i) stay working throughout the remainder of your notice period or (ii) go on paid leave effective immediately.If you continue to try to exit early, given the unparticularised nature of your allegations, &nbsp;we can only conclude that you are grasping for reasons to engineer such an exit for your own reasons, which is unprofessional, threatens breaches of your employment contract, and is not in the best interests of our clients.&nbsp; We put you on notice that we will not hesitate to take legal action against you to enforce your employment contract (in particular your notice period and all covenants), nor will we hesitate to take action against any firm that might seek to employ you ahead of your notice period expiring or in breach of your covenants.If you choose to remain working at the firm, we must insist that you focus solely on your work and only raise any further concerns with sufficient particularity and justification so that we can understand them fully and investigate them if necessary.&nbsp; Unclear and unparticularised allegations as you have been raising for the past several weeks are simply improper and must stop.Regarding the specific points raised in your emails:We are looking into your concerns over Gramercy’s recent input into the Litigation Management Agreement and Agency Agreements. &nbsp;Your email was lengthy, so we need time to fully digest your concerns, but we intend to respond early next week.&nbsp; For the avoidance of doubt, the remainder of this email was prepared before we received your email regarding Gramercy.Your suggestion that you cannot act in the best interests of our clients under supervision from other staff is not understood.&nbsp; If you continue to believe this is the case, please explain which members of staff and why, by precise reference to specific provisions of your contract or the SRA Code of Conduct, say this is so.You refer vaguely to potential criminal conduct.&nbsp; This is obviously a very serious allegation.&nbsp; Please now state clearly and unequivocally what precise conduct you are referring to and by which specific people so that we can investigate immediately.As you are aware, the firm has already taken robust action against Tom Goodhead.&nbsp; We take our obligations to our stakeholders extremely seriously and there is not, therefore, any basis for you to seek to exit early.&nbsp; Even if there has been improper behaviour at the Firm – and rest assured, we will investigate any such allegations seriously – that does not give you any justification, under either your contract or your regulatory obligations. Conjecture about what may or may not be published in The Times does not change that position.I look forward to hearing back from you regarding whether you wish to continue working on the case at PG or going onto paid leave by return and in any event by 5pm on Monday 20 October 2025. We remain hopeful that you will agree to continue to work at PG throughout the PDD Trial.In the meantime, and given your reference to protected disclosures and your suggestion that you will cease working on Monday despite the terms of your contract, please confirm that you have and will continue to preserve all documents that might be relevant to your employment with PG and associated covenants.All of the firm’s rights are fully reserved.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;&nbsp;James&nbsp;NewtonAssociateT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1016|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;78&nbsp;6063&nbsp;5157E:&nbsp;&nbsp;james.newton@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInPallas Partners LLP is a limited liability partnership registered in England with registered number OC437491, and is authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority of England and Wales (“SRA”) with SRA number 826251. A list of names of the members is available for inspection at our registered address at&nbsp;110 Bishopsgate, London, EC2N 4AY.&nbsp;The word “partner” denotes a member of&nbsp;Pallas Partners LLP&nbsp;or an employee or consultant with equivalent standing and qualifications.&nbsp;Pallas Partners (US) LLP is a limited liability partnership established in Delaware and registered in New York, located at 75 Rockefeller Plaza, New York, NY, 10019.&nbsp;Attorneys practicing law with Pallas Partners (US) LLP are admitted to practice in New York and their professional conduct is regulated by the New York Rules of Professional Conduct.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;This email (and any attachments) is confidential and may also be legally privileged and is intended solely for the use of the individual or entity addressed above. If you are not the intended recipient, please immediately notify the sender, then delete it from your system. You should not copy it or use it for any purpose, nor disclose its contents to any other person. Please also note that emails sent or received may be monitored to ensure compliance with the law and with our policies.&nbsp;Further regulatory information can be found in the Legal Notices which appear on our website at&nbsp;https://www.pallasllp.com/legal.​​​​From: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 17 October 2025 13:44To: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Urquhart, Charles &lt;charles.urquhart@clydeco.com&gt;Subject: RE: Report&nbsp;We will need to send them a complete response to this. Do you want Friston to take first crack at it, or us?&nbsp;Either way, I would today send a holding response this, stating that you are looking into this very long email and intending to respond to it next week. In the meantime, before anything is determined – and unanswered allegations in an email to them are not a determination – they must not without your permission raise this issue with the court, clients, other claimant firms or the defendants.&nbsp;I don’t think this needs to change the letter to Burke much, except reference to it needs to be added, and we obviously need to make clear that it is not retaliation for the disclosure. &nbsp;&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 17 October 2025 13:37To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Urquhart, Charles &lt;charles.urquhart@clydeco.com&gt;Subject: Re: Report&nbsp;Looping in Charlie and Raminder as well in light of our discussion and prediction. I wonder if we go to Mark F as he advised on the LMA and not Stewarts is my understanding.&nbsp;Attached is the chain where I 'instructed' Sarah to follow up - reading that email more carefully it is in fact suggesting control by Gramercy. I have not responded to that email yet but will do today.​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Friday, October 17, 2025 1:27 PMTo: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: Report &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOS​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Friday, October 17, 2025 1:22 pmTo:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Priyanka Gladson &lt;pgladson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Report &nbsp;Dear Board,&nbsp;We write further to the emails exchanged between Michael Burke, Sarah Bingham and Anna Varga dated 15 and 16 October 2025 as they relate to the Litigation Management Agreement (&quot;LMA&quot;)&nbsp;and Agency Agreement (&quot;AA&quot;). This email is intended to be a protected disclosure.&nbsp;&nbsp;As can be seen from the First Witness Statement of Alicia Alinia dated 30 September at paragraph 35.1 - she has confirmed (and verified with a statement of truth): &quot;For the avoidance of doubt, Gramercy has no control over the day-to-day management or decisions of the Firm or the Partner, and nor does Gramercy have any role in the conduct, control or management of the NOx Group Litigations.&quot;&nbsp;Further, at 35.3, it is confirmed that &quot;Its board of directors is entirely independent of Gramercy, and nothing in its financial arrangements inhibits the Firm from actively, and independently, pursuing the Proceedings in the best interests of its clients.&quot;&nbsp;On account of the email sent by Anna Varga on 16 October at 8.57AM in which she explicitly instructs Sarah Bingham to instruct Stewarts (who are retained by Gramercy - see email from Joshua Katz dated 13.05.2025 confirming this) to provide input into documents central to the NOx Litigation - the statement at 35.1 is now categorically untrue. Senior management has instructed a member of staff to engage with a firm which is instructed by Gramercy to review both Pan NOx and PG specific documents. This position therefore must be corrected to the Court and to the Defendants (and to the PG staff) where the firm have represented that Gramercy does not have input into the conduct of the&nbsp;Litigations (in&nbsp;the case of to the Court - with a signed statement of truth).&nbsp;&nbsp;With regard to 35.3 - see the email from Julian Chamberlayne on 9 September 2025 at 11.30 in which he confirms that &quot;I have now heard from Gramercy that, based on our review, they are content with you proceeding with the revised agency agreements&quot;&nbsp;. In circumstances where Stewarts, instructed by Gramercy, are reviewing and providing approval in respect of key NOx documents and requiring PG to await execution prior to their approval, it cannot be true to state that the Firm can independently pursue the Proceedings (and is in fact doing so) cannot be true.&nbsp;We completely understand that a litigation funder&nbsp;will have a legitimate interest in reviewing certain documents, and may quite properly wish to have input where those documents either (a) give rise to a financial liability on the funder, or (b) relate to compliance with the funding terms.We also acknowledge PG’s position under the funding arrangements in particular, the covenant requiring PG to obtain the funder’s prior approval before engaging any new law firm or barrister to whom PG grants a contingent interest. This requirement exists because such engagements could create a financial exposure that Gramercy may ultimately need to meet.However, the Pan-NOx Agency Agreement&nbsp;does not&nbsp;fall within that category. It does not create any contingent interests, nor does it involve any cost contribution obligations from the Non-Lead Firms. Its purpose is purely to define the principal–agent relationship&nbsp;between Pogust Goodhead (as Lead Solicitor) and the Non-Lead Firms, governing the conduct, management, strategy decisions and coordination of the litigation. In short, it enables PG to act independently as Lead Solicitor within the proceedings.Similarly, the Litigation Management Agreement is not a funding or liability document. Rather, it is an agreement between the Client Committee and Pogust Goodhead, setting out the instructions, authority and governance framework&nbsp;under which PG acts for the claimants within each GLO. It defines procedural and operational responsibilities, not financial exposure, and is an essential component of PG’s authority to manage the litigation.The level of control that Gramercy has sought to exercise over these documents &nbsp;which govern solicitor-client relationships, not funder obligations&nbsp; goes far beyond the usual parameters of a lender–borrower relationship. It represents an overreach into the conduct and management of the litigation itself, rather than oversight of financial risk. That distinction is fundamental, and Gramercy’s continued involvement in these matters strays beyond what is permissible for a funder maintaining a proper arm’s-length relationship with the litigation.It therefore&nbsp;appears that our collective position is that PG is&nbsp;now openly operating in a world where the funder of the firm has direct management/control of aspects of the litigation - and that control is on-going, despite representations&nbsp;to the contrary made to the Court, the Defendants and to the staff. This creates significant issues for the staff working on these Litigations both in our duties to our clients and to the clients of the other firms in our firm's role as Lead Solicitors.&nbsp;&nbsp;Can you please advise on the following:&nbsp;why representations have been made to the Court, Defendants and staff that Gramercy do not have any role in the conduct, control or management of the NOx Group Litigations when plainly - they do and continue to do so;whether the Board intends to update the Court as to the true position; andwhether the Board intends to inform the clients and other claimant firms of Gramercy's input into documents that have a direct bearing on costs and client instructions.&nbsp;We are continuing to consider this on-going issue as more information comes to light. All of our rights are reserved.&nbsp;&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael, Priyanka, Sarah&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344&nbsp;_____________________________________________________ If our account details change, we will notify these to you by letter, telephone or face-to-face and never by email. Clyde &amp; Co’s privacy notice can be found here Privacy notice: Clyde &amp; Co (clydeco.com) Please could we request that all correspondence with us is sent electronically where possible. For matters subject to the jurisdiction of England &amp; Wales and where you have agreed with the lawyer with the conduct of the case that email service is appropriate, please use this address service@clydeco.com for service, subject to the restrictions set out here . Please copy your email to the lawyer with conduct of the case and include our Clyde &amp; Co reference. This email is sent for and on behalf of Clyde &amp; Co LLP, a limited liability partnership registered in England and Wales under number OC326539 and with its registered office at The St Botolph Building, 138 Houndsditch, London, EC3A 7AR, United Kingdom (Tel: +44 20 7876 5000. Fax: +44 20 7876 5111). Clyde &amp; Co LLP is authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority under number 460690 and uses the word &quot;partner&quot; to refer to a member of the LLP, or an employee or consultant with equivalent standing and qualifications. A list of members is available at: www.clydeco.com. This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you have received this message in error, please notify the sender immediately, destroy this email and any attachments, and do not use, copy, store and/or disclose to any person this email and any attachments. "}

