Pls see draft response for Mike for your review (the rest will be along the same lines). &nbsp;I can send it from me if you are ok with this. …………………………………………….Dear Michael&nbsp;Thank you for your resignation email dated 15th September 2025.&nbsp;It’s disappointing to note that you have chosen to resign given that the Board have listened to concerns which have been raised and have engaged in a process to allay them.&nbsp; We also note the concerns you raise related to the previous leadership of the firm. The new Board are determined to bring the highest standards of propriety and integrity to the organisation&nbsp; and are confident that the process being undertaken will arrive at a place that will be in the best interests of the Firm, its employees and, most importantly, its clients. Given the above process, your resignation seems premature. As a result, it is with regret, we accept it.&nbsp;The Firm notes your request for an early release and also your acceptance of your obligations at clause 16 of your resignation letter. Given the deadlines involved in the case you referred to, at this stage the Firm would like you to continue working your notice to ensure that the clients are not put at a disadvantage as a result of your decision. To the same end, and at an appropriate point, we would like you to undertake an orderly handover of your files. At that point the Firm would be happy to discuss an appropriate way forward with you. Please continue working normally in the meantime.&nbsp;Please note that the entirety of your contract of employment remains in place during your notice period. This includes the express obligations set out under clauses 4.2, 16, 17 and 21&nbsp;of the employment contract executed by you with a commencement date of 1st September 2022. Your contract also contains implicit contractual obligations as to “good faith and fidelity.”&nbsp; This includes an obligation to act honestly in all dealings with your employer, not working (or conspiring) with a competitor, not disclosing our confidential information or trade secrets, not actively disrupting the business or enticing colleagues or clients to leave.&nbsp; To this end it is notable that a number of your colleagues have chosen to resign contemporaneously.&nbsp; Please be aware that the company will not hesitate to take robust action to enforce any breach of your obligations up to an including court action if that becomes necessary. I also bring your attention more generally to the fact that the restrictive covenants at clause 21 of your employment contract, which were varied by your agreement on 14th September 2023, continue to remain in effect for up to 6 months after your effective date of termination.&nbsp;If you should have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From: Anna Terry &lt;aterry@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Monday, 15 September 2025 at 10:45To: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: Notice of Resignation&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;Terry(She/Her)Executive&nbsp;Assistant+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7436&nbsp;336&nbsp;078From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Monday, September 15, 2025 10:24To:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;HR Team &lt;hr@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Notice of Resignation&nbsp;Dear Board and HR,&nbsp;Please see attached my notice of resignation.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344&nbsp;"}

