fice at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Priscilla Mendes &lt;pmendes@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 05 October 2025 21:56To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dunford, Kit &lt;Kit.Dunford@fticonsulting.com&gt;; Paula Razera &lt;prazera@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Dougie Inglis &lt;dInglis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Strat Comm Pogust Goodhead &lt;pogustgoodhead@fticonsulting.com&gt;Subject: Re: Comms prep - NOx PTR&nbsp;Hi Alicia,&nbsp;Please find attached the memo, which was prepared before the recent leadership changes in the case. It is intended for sharing with journalists interested in the claim – we have this kind of memo for all LATAM cases, as a set of pre-approved wording in place is important to streamline press requests and avoid reverting to Legal each time a new enquiry arises.&nbsp;In preparation for tomorrow’s PTR, my team has also reviewed the Defendant’s skeleton and compiled a note highlighting all mentions of PG that could present PR issues or risks – also attached.&nbsp;If Kit/FTI or Pallas have visibility on the strategy behind PG’s application to step down, it would be very helpful have their views - as my team and I have not been involved in these discussions to date&nbsp;Lastly, we received a request this afternoon from Alistair Gray, from FT, asking for a copy of PG’s skeleton for the PTR. As I understand it will only be on public domain once the