 Our budgets were exchanged with the Defendants on 17 June and we have been considering them since. We are due to provide a response to the Defendants budgets in documents knows as Budget Discussion Report (“BDRs”) on 3 July and we are working with our
 counsel team to prepare these now. We image the BDRs may assist in bring about more agreement with the Defendants and in advance of skeleton arguments which are due on 10 July 2025.


Again, we will keep you updated on this hearing as we progress towards it.


Pre-Trial Review&nbsp;(“PTR”)


The final hearing in July and before the summer break is the PTR. Generally this hearing is reserved for procedural matters, including timetabling
 for the main trial, the running order of issues and the trial bundle, as opposed to any more substantive issues between the parties.


However, in these cases which are extraordinary, it is likely that this PTR will deal with a larger number of issues including any final applications
