Thanks Matt, Alessia.&nbsp;Please see attached the 24 Sept letter referred to in the Renault notice Alessia asked for. &nbsp;Additionally, noting that the Renault application asked for confirmation by 4pm of whether we could provide the request information, we have prepared the short draft email below. If we’re not able to get the broader letter to the Defendants out in the next hour, we’d propose sending this by way of interim response. Do let us know if you have any thoughts. &nbsp;Jess &nbsp;***********************************&nbsp;Dear Sirs/Madams, &nbsp;We acknowledge receipt of Renault’s request for information regarding the individual within Pogust Goodhead has assumed overall responsibility for the Emissions litigation.&nbsp;We confirm that we propose to share an update with the Defendant firms addressing this point in advance of the stated deadline of noon on 25 September 2025. &nbsp;On this basis, we confirm that there is no need for Renault to issue the application notice. &nbsp;&nbsp;Yours faithfully &nbsp;Pogust Goodhead&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 14:45To: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Draft email to Ds on stepping down&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Thanks Jessica. It sounds very positive.&nbsp;Would you like us to write up the detailed heads of terms?&nbsp;When we get back your comments on the witness statement, we will update it to take account of these developments (just the progress to agreement, not the details).&nbsp;We will also look at the Freshfields letter and consider if we need to refer to it now (probably not), or deal with it later.&nbsp;Matt&nbsp;&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 14:26To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Draft email to Ds on stepping down&nbsp;All, &nbsp;Please see below a summary of the call with LD at 1.15. Other than PG it was just Martyn and Sapna from LD, Lizzy Comley (S&amp;G) and Edward Cardington. Please also see attached Anna’s email to Martyn following this call which summarises the agreed points. In particular, please note that it was proposed to agree some broad heads of terms in advance of an agreement on the practical details next week. &nbsp;Separately, we have just received the attached letter from Freshfields, which we are considering in parallel. &nbsp;BestJess&nbsp;****************Note from call with Leigh Day and Slater &amp; Gordon &nbsp;Seconding case leads We stated our firm position that we no PG staff and in particular none of the case leads should be seconded out of the firm. In particular AA stated that in light of the decision to step down as Lead Sols, and in light of Renault’s application being innocuous, there was no need for this action. AA also referenced the individuals’ professional obligations to the clients. Martyn acknowledged our position, and that he could not force us to take that step. He suggested we send the letter to the Defendants re stepping down and see what the response is. Said to keep it under review. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Costs Martyn agreed that there “wasn’t the slightest chance” of LD agreeing common costs without PG’s agreement. Stated that PG and LD were in a joint enterprise.On costs protection – we sought confirmation from LD on the wording in the agency agreement “protection against liability for common work”. Martyn stated that once PG are no longer Lead Sols they would not anticipate coming to PG for approval, but would involve everyone in the discussion. We said that given the broader SteerCo context, we could let go of “express approval”&nbsp;Relationship between PG &amp; LD Martyn stated that LD is “desperately in need” of the PG team and would want the PG team working on the case as normal. Stated that once this is resolved he would totally support PG coming back in. PG welcomed and echoed these sentiments. &nbsp;Next steps We stated that the letter to the Defendants would be sent ASAP, and that the application would follow hopefully today / possibly tomorrow. Lizzy (Slater &amp; Gordon) suggested that they could share a headline agreement for PG to see before formally stepping down (in advance of a more detailed agreement next week)A call was proposed for Monday or Tuesday next week to discuss nuts and bolts of how PG’s step down / ongoing work with LD would work in practice. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Please note that our general terms and conditions apply to all our services. These general terms and conditions include a clause stipulating that our liability is excluded for damage