.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: Re: Draft email to Ds on stepping down&nbsp;All&nbsp;Re the guardrail proposals: had some feedback. A call will be taking place with the Steer Co today to go through the proposed guardrails options. The key sticking point is where the &quot;senior team will be&quot; as they &quot;cannot be at PG&quot;. Martyn is suggesting this was agreed - it was not - it was discussed nothing more. Of course, it also begs the question of what happens with my role.&nbsp;&nbsp;@Alicia Alinia&nbsp;call been proposed for 12.45 - I cannot do that but could anytime from 1pm - are you free for that? Would be good to lock this in asap.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pallas - I will share the feedback re the proposals - please could have a session where we run through this so we can identify lines in the sand. I dont want to be ambushed and there is a risk of that in terms of information/knowledge asymmetry.&nbsp;&nbsp;I need to communicate to the wider Nox team that we are stepping before that letter goes to Ds.&nbsp;Anna&lt;image002.png&gt;​​​​&lt;image003.png&gt;Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Thursday, September 25, 2025 10:03 AMTo: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Draft email to Ds on stepping down &nbsp;All, &nbsp;Further to the below, please see attached the draft correspondence to the Ds on stepping down, now in letter format. We are updating in parallel to ensure that all Defendants are included as addressees. &nbsp;You can also access a live version of the doc here: &nbsp;&lt;image004.png&gt;&nbsp;Draft Letter from PG to Defendant Firms (2025-09-25).docx &nbsp;Please could you let us know if there are any final comments? Kind RegardsJess &nbsp;&lt;image002.png&gt;​​​​&lt;image003.png&gt;Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 24 September 2025 20:39To: Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Draft email to Ds on stepping down&nbsp;You don't often get email from matthew.getz@pallasllp.com. Learn why this is important CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Anna&nbsp;Please see beneath a draft email to Ds on stepping down. We include options of if we have LD/SC agreement and if we do not.&nbsp;We can take a view in the morning if it should be sent in either version, or revised again to take account of developments.&nbsp;Matt&nbsp;---------------&nbsp;Dear Defendants’ Solicitors,As solicitors representing a group of 750,000 claimants in the NOx Litigations, we are constantly vigilant to ensure that we are acting in the best interests of our clients and to forward the efficient case management of this important litigation.With that in mind, and in view of the various allegations that the Defendants have advanced, we have determined that our continued status as Lead Solicitors across the Lead Cases, and the focus put on us as a firm in this role, is causing unnecessary distractions, at least in the current moment, and threatening to imperil the trial. Therefore, we are writing to inform you of our intention in principle to resign as Lead Solicitors from the Lead Cases on a temporary basis for the duration of the liability trial. This should not be taken as acceptance that any of your recent criticisms about the Firm’s capacity to conduct this work in a responsible, compliant fashion are correct. We stand by our position in the letter to you dated 23 September 2025.We shall continue to work diligently on behalf of our clients, and will remain as a member of the Mercedes Sterring Committee.&nbsp; We will also conduct the necessary trial work as authorised &nbsp;by the remaining Lead Solicitors and/or the Steering Committee (as the case may be), as explicitly authorised by the Court in the applicable Group Litigation Orders (the “GLOs”).[The Lead Solicitors, Steering Committee [and Claimant Solicitors Groups] have all agreed with our proposal.]OR[The Lead Solicitors and Steering Committee are considering our proposal, and we expect agreement soon.][Only if we have agreement in principle] To ensure we continue to act in the best interests of our clients, the precise terms of our stepping back are currently being finalised and documented between the relevant Claimants’ legal representatives. To the extent appropriate and relevant, we will provide further confirmation to you as soon as practicable after final agreement is reached. [If we have some details of what is agreed with LD/SC, and we think it appropriate, we can share it now.]There will also be a need to amend certain mechanics of the GLOs. We will be issuing an application in this regard as soon as possible. We presume it can be agreed by consent.Finally, we note that some of you had raised the issue of our status as Lead Solicitor or potential Lead Solicitor (see the letters of HSFKL on 16 September 2025 and the letter of CGSH to Milberg on 11 September 2025), and were potentially considering applying for an order in respect thereof at the Pre Trial Review. Clearly, any such application would now be a waste of court and party time, and should not be issued.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;GetzPartner&lt;image001.png&gt;T:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInPallas Partners LLP is a limited liability partnership registered in England with registered number OC437491, and is authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority of England and Wales (“SRA”) with SRA number 826251. A list of names of the members is available for inspection at our registered address at&nbsp;110 Bishopsgate, London, EC2N 4AY.&nbsp;The word “partner” denotes a member of&nbsp;Pallas Partners LLP&nbsp;or an employee or consultant with equivalent standing and qualifications.&nbsp;Pallas Partners (US) LLP is a limited liability partnership established in Delaware and registered in New York, located at 75 Rockefeller Plaza, New York, NY, 10019.&nbsp;Attorneys practicing law with Pallas Partners (US) LLP are admitted to practice in New York and their professional conduct is regulated by the New York Rules of Professional Conduct.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;This email (and any attachments) is confidential and may also be legally privileged and is intended solely for the use of the individual or entity addressed above. If you are not the intended recipient, please immediately notify the sender, then delete it from your system. You should not copy it or use it for any purpose, nor disclose its contents to any other person. Please also note that emails sent or received may be monitored to ensure compliance with the law and with our policies.&nbsp;Further regulatory information can be found in the Legal Notices which appear on our website at&nbsp;https://www.pallasllp.com/legal.​​​​&nbsp;&lt;Draft Letter from PG to Defendant Firms (2025-09-25).docx&gt;"}

