Dear All,
&nbsp;
+ 
@Sarah
Thank you all for your time and candour yesterday.
I am deeply conscious of the impact the past weeks have had on you. They follow many months of extraordinary effort in the lead-up to trial, during which I know each of you has made real personal sacrifices with friends and loved ones. The pace has been
 relentless, and I recognise how draining that is.
On top of this, we’ve all had to contend with the heightened scrutiny on our work and the damaging leaks from those who chose to undermine our integrity. I won’t suggest the road ahead will be easy, nor that trust will be restored overnight. What I can promise
 is that Joe, Howard and I are committed, wholeheartedly, to acting in the best interests of this firm and our clients, and we will demonstrate that in the weeks to come.
I also want to acknowledge that there are long-standing conversations still to be had, particularly around incentives for you and your teams, which have been spoken of for some time but not delivered. These are important discussions, and I want to have them
 with you. At the same time, I fully respect that after the intensity of recent months and certainly the past few weeks, you may need space before engaging on these issues. Please know that I will not press for those conversations until you feel ready.
We are, undeniably, under intense pressure. In moments like these, what matters most is our shared responsibility to our clients and to each other. That responsibility includes upholding the commitments we have made, both to those we serve and to one another.
 If at any point someone decides their journey should continue outside the firm, that decision will of course be respected. But with that choice comes the responsibility to honour the contractual obligations and covenants we each carry. These aren’t abstract
 rules, they are essential safeguards that protect our clients and preserve the integrity of the work we have built together. Upholding them is not simply a legal duty but a reflection of our professionalism and the values we stand for.
Thank you again for your resilience, your professionalism, and your dedication. It is because of you that we are able to continue this work with purpose and strength.
Best wishes, 
A
