Subject: PG secondment


&nbsp;

Alicia, Howard, Joseph, Anna,


&nbsp;


We were earlier informed, in a meeting with Martyn Day, that the PG Board, LD and counsel, have constructed a proposed &quot;secondment&quot;&nbsp;of
 the emissions case leads and some other colleagues to Leigh Day, at least on a temporary basis.&nbsp; We were informed that the &quot;secondment&quot; is to be set out in a witness statement due this evening, and a (presumably disclosable) side letter/ agency agreement,
 assuming that we (being those subject to the &quot;secondment&quot;)&nbsp;agree to the secondment and statement.&nbsp; We were informed that this proposal arises out meetings&nbsp;with counsel last Friday 26 September&nbsp;and this morning, Monday 29 September. It is unclear whether this
 would also require an amendment to our contracts, or whether the firm intended to seek our consent to do this.


&nbsp;


We should have been invited to those&nbsp;meetings.&nbsp; Not involving us in discussions in relation to our future, and the future of the trial,
 is unhelpful and distressing, and significantly adversely impacts our ability to focus on the trial.&nbsp; It also does not make sense to exclude from meetings about trial strategy the PG case leads who have been responsible for trial preparation and strategy for
 years (and still are responsible).&nbsp; Please include us in all similar meetings.


&nbsp;


We are concerned that the very nature of the proposed secondment signals to the Court and Defendants that there are in fact legitimate
 concerns over funder control; it begs the question why would the secondment be necessary if there was nothing to worry about?&nbsp; It therefore risks exacerbating the problem it pretends to solve.


&nbsp;


It seems to us (including Sarah) that the most sensible solution is to engage in constructive discussions directly with us so as to
 negate impact on the PDD Trial and quantum work streams as far as possible.


&nbsp;


Please let us know your availability for a meeting to discuss.&nbsp; That meeting should ideally be today, given that we understand a witness
 statement explaining the secondment is to be served this evening, taking into account availability.
&nbsp;
Michael, Priyanka, Sarah, Matt, Georgie

































