Dear all,

&nbsp;
We would be grateful for views on next steps in relation to costs of the de-designation applications/hearing.

&nbsp;
Summary of the current position

&nbsp;
As a reminder, paragraph 19 of the Order dated 29 August 2025 states:

&nbsp;
The Claimants’ costs of the De-Designation Hearing shall be summarily assessed if not agreed, on the standard basis. The Lead Defendants shall pay one
 third of these costs forthwith, with the balance to be costs in the case. Two thirds of the Lead Defendants’ costs to be costs in the case, subject to assessment on the standard basis.

&nbsp;
The Claimants' Statement of Costs totals £1,649,246.80. One third of that amount is £549,748.93. Ds have made significant complaints about our costs in open correspondence. We responded
 on 5 November in open and also made the following WPSATC offer (see attached): 

&nbsp;

The Lead Defendants shall make an interim payment in the sum of £302,361.91, representing 55% of one third of the Claimants'
 costs. The balance of 45% of one third to be summarily assessed if not agreed, on the standard basis;
or
&nbsp;

The Lead Defendants make payment in the sum of £412,311.70, representing 75% of one third of the Claimants’ costs, in
 full and final settlement of the costs payable forthwith pursuant to paragraph 19 of the Order.

&nbsp;
The remaining two-thirds of the Claimants' costs, amounting to £1,099,497.87, shall be treated as costs in the case, subject to assessment on the standard
 basis in due course. 
&nbsp;
Ds have now responded offering £700,000 (c.42% of our claimed costs) with £233,333 payable forthwith, and the remainder of £466,667 being costs in the case. The deadline for accepting
 this offer was Friday 5 December (which hopefully is not too much of an issue because I don’t think we would have accepted it in any event).

&nbsp;
The relevant correspondence is attached, along with a note of the LD/PG con on 17 October 2025.

